{"title":"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(slower)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (slower)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(quicker)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (quicker)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2.5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2.5</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a ring toss game at a carnival, three rings are tossed over any of three pegs. A ring over peg A is worth <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/289ab29fa1f322171e782b23b50d8d91fefbc265.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$one$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"10\" /> point, over peg B <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a43c290783cafb453134016474b6595d2fbbb67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$three$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> points and over peg C <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/a/45a0053a65160ce1d9cde72e5a0724476ea67c2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$five$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> points. If all three rings land on pegs, how many different point totals are possible? (It is possible to have more than one ring on a peg.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/a/88ad2a8d37f06e2db581c41a718017ab5f77a33a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)} 12 \\quad\\text{(B)} 7\\quad \\text{(C)} 10\\quad \\text{(D)} 13 \\quad \\text{(E)} 6 \\quad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"282\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28slower.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(slower)\">Solution 1 (slower)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (slower)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can list all of the possible sums. We can also disregard cases where the points are swapped around because the totals will be the same.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/585788df1d33882aeb1371884ad082a7724ed395.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 1 + 1 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible point totals so far\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6bc236cf7241be50e147c020e428431daccf85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 1 + 3 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible point totals so far\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f598bac8a01c3423a221a192b3ec7370a5708c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 1 + 5 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible point totals so far\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/6/2360689fb62b67bf098892dff838c10ae2a99ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 3 + 3 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />. However, this is the same as a previous value, so we don't count it.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e46e30e3c45a73f2f3eeb1afb8f7b3c87cdde2d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 3 + 5 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible point totals so far\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/b/ebb133b3bdf952e3b9863ac93001b17b4812b94e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 3 + 5 = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible point totals so far\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a84bb601a941b16104f38900c7a4d580ad7096de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 5 + 5 = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible point totals so far\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/1/021022e1337ceb525874baccfc1f4fb4c2ea88c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + 5 + 5 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible point totals so far.\n</p><p>All of the other possible arrangements are just re-orderings, so we can see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de65dba55d14d8e931640744213df830f51dbd18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" /> possible point totals.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28quicker.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(quicker)\">Solution 2 (quicker)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (quicker)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can figure out that the lowest point total is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the smallest total would be getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> three times and that the largest value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because the largest total would be getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> three times. We also can realize that all of the possible point values must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> apart because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> apart. This means that you can increase the point value by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by changing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, we can now list all of the point values:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/0/a60e1c45e02831342d902396cc0f84cef435b5be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>We can see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/6/de65dba55d14d8e931640744213df830f51dbd18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" /> possible point totals.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2.5\">Solution 2.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the same first starting steps until . However, instead of listing all of the point totals, we can use the first and last term, as well as the common difference between the terms, to figure out how many possible point totals there are. From solution 2, the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the last term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and the common difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We can use translations to produce a new sequence and subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from each term so that the first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the last term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Since the common difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can now see that the number of point totals is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f89d78cafce5c5619b48b7765b515f615e4d32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 = 1 \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/a/59a3c2ae9185b200b6ec66773d23656e83483a9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 = 7 \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, and so the number of point totals is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/24078dec8587f09aa914c026c3e7a66f2352fda0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 - 1 + 1 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"153\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 25 (page does not exist)\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017191730\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.094 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 305/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2333/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 593/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8359/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    9.258      1 Template:CEMC_box\n100.00%    9.258      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:34963:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017191730 and revision id 271767. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}